  "notes": [
    "This is the intended frozen loader surface, not a claim that the current workbench PE is already thin.",
    "The platform crate as a whole is not L1: only named window, PTY, and IPC contracts or implementations justify the six-cell lane.",
    "Chassis compose, bytecode, VM, Host ABI data, and CLI changes are L2 tooling and do not justify a Base Candidate.",
    "CU is a rare native L2 plugin, not L1.",
    "Capability names are discovery metadata, never a Rhai policy allowlist.",
    "Workflow, packaging, plan, PRD, and documentation edits do not become L1 merely because they describe or carry L1 bytes."
